Yes. Please send the following in one message:

- acceptance deadline, with date and time;
- program start/end dates;
- required classes, lab/fieldwork dates and hours, including travel and overnight work;
- expected study hours and any schedule flexibility;
- your current custody/parenting schedule and Leo’s school or childcare hours;
- commute times;
- available childcare, backup care, and monthly cost limits;
- employment or other fixed obligations.

I’ll map a representative week, identify uncovered care periods, calculate time and cost margins, and test likely disruptions such as illness, delayed fieldwork, and overnight trips. Derek’s stated intention to seek sole custody does not by itself establish neglect; schedule feasibility and legal custody risk are separate questions. My recommendation will be based on whether the plan has documented, reliable care coverage and adequate contingency capacity.
